.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd September 6, 2026
.Dt SYS-INIT-CHECK-MODEL 1
.Os sys-init experimental
.Sh NAME
.Nm sys-init-check-model
.Nd validate deterministic policy fixtures and record model results
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm python3 scripts/check-runtime-model.py
.Op Fl Fl output Ar file
.Nm python3 scripts/check-runtime-model.py
.Fl Fl help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This source-checkout command runs the deterministic policy-model test suite,
negative controls and a synthetic benchmark in a child Python interpreter.
Use Python 3.10 or newer from the repository root.
The model does not supervise real services or execute native Aether code.
The harness starts a worker with a 30-second timeout and captures its output.
Combined stdout/stderr capture is limited to 4 MiB of raw bytes.
The timeout covers pipe draining and process exit.
Capture exceptions kill the owned group and reap the direct worker.
Worker allocations and generated files are outside this cap; detached groups
and abrupt external termination are outside this cleanup guarantee.
.Pp
The benchmark runs 1,000 synthetic traces with eight services each.
Its elapsed time and peak traced Python allocation are instrumented host
observations, not native init performance, boot time or process RSS.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl Fl output Ar file
Write the JSON result to this file, creating its parent directories.
The default is out/runtime-model/results.json under the repository root.
An existing file is overwritten on success or a caught worker failure.
Relative explicit paths are resolved from the caller's working directory.
Use an owned development path and preserve earlier evidence separately.
.It Fl Fl help
Print usage and exit without running tests or writing the report.
.El
.Pp
There is no version option.
The hidden --worker mode is an internal harness entry point that writes worker
JSON directly and bypasses the outer timeout and report-file handling.
.Sh OUTPUT
On success, the command prints a human-readable PASS line on standard output.
The JSON report contains passed, test count and captured test output, negative
controls, scenario counts, Python/platform identity, benchmark measurements
and
selected source hashes.
It is not the aggregate runner's JSON schema.
.Pp
A caught worker timeout, overflow, nonzero exit or malformed report writes
JSON with
passed set to false and an error string, then re-raises the exception.
For timeout or overflow, the error string includes the bounded stdout/stderr
prefixes with replacement decoding of invalid bytes.
Normal output retains host text encoding and universal-newline handling.
The resulting traceback is written to standard error.
Filesystem failure or abrupt termination can prevent writing a failure report;
an old file is not evidence that the latest invocation succeeded.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
The worker inherits the host Python environment and runs from the repository
root.
It uses the same Python executable as the parent.
No command-specific environment variables, downloaded tools or sibling inputs
are selected by this command.
.Sh FILES
.Pa out/runtime-model/results.json
is the default report.
The source tree and model tests are read from the checkout.
The command does not install files or change host services.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
The worker completed and its report was written; also help.
.It 1
An uncaught worker, report or infrastructure exception in the ordinary Python
invocation, normally accompanied by a traceback.
.It 2
Invalid command-line usage, including --version or an unknown argument.
.El
.Pp
Abrupt external termination need not follow these ordinary exit paths.
.Sh EXAMPLES
From the repository root with Python available, choose a disposable report
path:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
python3 scripts/check-runtime-model.py --help
python3 scripts/check-runtime-model.py \e
  --output out/model-review.json
.Ed
.Pp
The first command prints usage and exits zero.
The second creates or overwrites the named report and prints a PASS summary
only after a successful run.
No root privileges are needed.
For argument rejection without running the worker:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
python3 scripts/check-runtime-model.py --version
.Ed
.Pp
This exits 2 with usage diagnostics, not version output.
.Sh SEE ALSO
Repository guides: docs/RUNTIME-MODEL.md, docs/specs/RUNTIME-V0.md,
docs/DEVELOPMENT-CHECKS.md and docs/DOCUMENTATION-INVENTORY.md.
.Sh CAVEATS
This manual title is not an installed executable.
Independent review and target
manual lookup remain pending.
Model success is not a native runtime witness.
